      en: "The Ismoil Somoni Monument, located in the central Dusti Square in Dushanbe, is the most significant national symbol of Tajikistan, established in 1999 to honor the 1100th anniversary of the Samanid Empire. The statue depicts Ismoil Somoni, the founder of the Samanid Dynasty, who ruled over a vast and culturally prosperous Central Asian territory during the 9th and 10th centuries. The monument features a grand gilded statue of the ruler standing proudly beneath a magnificent 40-meter-high arch, which is intricately adorned with gold leaf and precious stones. Somoni holds a scepter topped by a crown with seven stars, symbolizing the enduring unity of the Tajik nation and its seven historic regions. The architectural ensemble, flanked by two large bronze lions representing strength and sovereignty, merges classical Oriental forms with contemporary Tajik design elements. It serves as the primary site for major state ceremonies, military parades, and high-level diplomatic visits in the capital. Ismoil Somoni's legacy is absolutely central to the country's modern national identity, as he is credited with establishing a centralized Tajik state, and even the national currency was named in his honor.",
